 out while that mortgage was still  in place if that happens all you need to  do is get the owner to ask for a letter  of consent which normally they'll do  because normally the lender especially  if there's been a change of  circumstances with the owner normally  the lender just wants their uh interest  paid so with a letter of consent you  don't have to refinance you can rent the  property out sometimes they say no in  which case you might just have to find  another property hope that helps  okay lucie should i do brr method in a  place as london where i'm starting out  or should i do it in a cheaper place  with cheaper houses starting out okay so  if you're doing a buy refurbished  refinance deal it does work in london or  the outskirts of london very well it  also works in cheaper areas some pros  and cons i'll say is the pros of doing  it near london is number one you live  there so you're gonna be able to manage  the property easier and also you know  the area well and you need to know the  area well  the cons of doing it in or around london  is houses are really expensive so you're  gonna probably need more money initially  to put down up front even though you'll  hopefully get it back up on the  refinance but also when you do refinance  it might be that the rent doesn't really  cover the mortgage because houses are so  expensive around london so it might be  better starting off further up north you  get the experience up north you'll be  able to get more cash flow and then once  you've understand the strategy and  you've done it potentially consider  moving  closer to home but there really are pros  and cons to each so i would just say  make sure you're comfortable you know  the area well and ultimately the numbers  stack up  if you enjoyed the video by the way  don't forget to hit like  okay top man says hi samuel i don't feel  good raising rents on current tenants  i feel you bro i do feel you  will i lose a lot of money not doing  this or will the increas